# Mexican Spanish Copy

VIDA speaks to Mexican tier-1 hourly workers — warehouse, maquiladora, factory, service, retail. 25–50, high-school education, phone-first.

## i18n setup (as of 2026-04-19)

- Library: **i18next + react-i18next** (v16)
- Translation files: `src/i18n/es.json` (canonical) and `src/i18n/en.json` (fallback for admin users)
- Init: `src/i18n/index.ts` — sets `<html lang>` on language change, persists to `localStorage.vida_lang`
- Keys are **flat, snake_case, prefix-first**: `nav_employers`, `hero_h1`, `chip_24hrs`, `phone_available`

**When adding new strings:**
1. Add to `es.json` first with the correct Mexican Spanish (see voice rules below)
2. Add to `en.json` with the same key
3. Use via `const { t } = useTranslation(); t('your_key')`
4. Ship the strings in the same PR as the UI using them

## Voice & register

- **Informal "tú", always.** "Tus datos", "tu préstamo", "te invitamos". Never "usted".
- **Short sentences.** Max ~16 words. Split anything longer.
- **Active voice.** "Solicita tu préstamo", not "Tu préstamo puede ser solicitado".
- **Direct, not euphemistic.** "Rechazado" over "no aprobado en este momento". Respect by being honest.
- **Warm but serious.** Money is involved. One `!` per page max.
- **Mexican, not Spain-ish.** "Celular" (not "móvil"), "carro" (not "coche" in casual), "platicar" (not "hablar" in casual).

## Vocabulary

### Banking/money

| Use | Avoid | Why |
|---|---|---|
| préstamo | crédito, mutuo | Plain word users recognize |
| solicitar | pedir, requerir | Expected verb for applying |
| monto | cantidad, suma | Industry-standard |
| cuota | mensualidad (OK) | Short, clear |
| saldo | balance (Spanglish) | Proper Spanish |
| plazo | tiempo | Financial-specific |
| tasa de interés | intereses (OK in body) | Regulatory term |
| CAT | — | Explain on first use: "Costo Anual Total, o CAT" |
| nómina | sueldo, paga | "Nómina" = payroll, precise |
| deducción | descuento | "Deducción" correct for payroll |
| descontar de tu nómina | sacar de tu sueldo | Precise + clean |

### Identity

| Use | Avoid |
|---|---|
| empleador | empresa, jefe, patrón |
| trabajador / empleado | obrero (demeaning), colaborador (corporate) |
| nombre completo | nombres y apellidos |
| teléfono celular | número de teléfono |
| CURP, RFC, CLABE | never rename to "código" |

## Formatting

- **Peso amounts:** `$5,000` (symbol + comma thousands). Never `MXN 5,000` inline. OK in legal footer.
- **Percentages:** `36%` (no space before `%`)
- **CAT/rates:** `CAT 45.2%` (one decimal)
- **Dates:** `15 de mayo de 2026` in prose, `15/05/2026` in tight UI
- **Phone:** `+52 55 1234 5678`

### Currency display

- Always currency context — never a bare "5000"
- Cents omitted by default, shown when present: `$5,000` vs `$5,000.50`
- Tabular nums: `<span className="tabular-nums">{formatPesos(n)}</span>`

### Sentence case, not Title Case

- "Solicitar préstamo" (good)
- "Solicitar Préstamo" (bad)

Capitalize only the first word + proper nouns.

### Punctuation

- **Inverted marks required:** `¿Cuál es tu CURP?`, `¡Bienvenido!` — never drop `¿` or `¡`
- **No serial comma in Spanish.** "Nombre, edad y teléfono" — not "nombre, edad, y teléfono"
- **Ellipsis:** single `…` char, not `...`
- **Quotes:** `"..."` (straight double)

## Existing good examples from es.json

Reference these when writing new copy:

```
"hero_h1": "Tu respaldo <em>financiero</em> integrado."
"hero_sub": "Liquidez de emergencia a través de la nómina de tu empleador. Pre-aprobado. Instantáneo."
"hero_cta_employer": "Soy Empleador"
"hero_cta_employee": "Soy Empleado"
"phone_available": "Crédito Disponible"
"phone_currency": "Pesos Mexicanos · Vía nómina"
"chip_24hrs": "24 hrs"
"chip_0fees": "$0 comisiones"
"ben_fees": "Comisiones ocultas"
```

Note: the hero uses `<em>` tags rendered via `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`. This is established; don't disrupt for a single fix.

## Don't

- No emoji in UI — juvenile for financial product. Icons via SVG.
- No gringo-ismos: "resetear", "customizar", "deletear". Use "reiniciar", "personalizar", "eliminar"
- No anglicisms in core flows: "login" → "Iniciar sesión", "logout" → "Cerrar sesión", "signup" → "Crear cuenta" or "Regístrate". ("Dashboard" widely used, acceptable)
- No legal jargon in UX copy. "Declaración contractual" → "Firma tu contrato"
- No vague errors. "Algo no está bien" → specific: "El CURP debe tener 18 caracteres"
- No "Lo sentimos" spam
- No "Haz clic aquí" — link text describes destination

## Regulatory-mandated copy

Per CNBV/CONDUSEF rules, preserve verbatim — don't improve:

- **CAT disclosure:** `Costo Anual Total (CAT) promedio [X]% sin IVA. Informativo. Fecha de cálculo: [fecha]. Vigente hasta [fecha].`
- **SOFOM identifier:** `VIDA Finance SOFOM, E.N.R. Sociedad Financiera de Objeto Múltiple, Entidad No Regulada. La inscripción en el Registro no implica certificado de solvencia.`
- **CONDUSEF link in footer:** `Para dudas compara en el portal de CONDUSEF: https://www.condusef.gob.mx`

If unsure whether copy is regulated → ask Isaac, don't change.

## Status/state message templates

| Event | Spanish copy |
|---|---|
| Loan approved | Tu préstamo fue aprobado |
| In manual review | Estamos revisando tu solicitud. Te avisamos en máximo 24 horas. |
| Rejected | No pudimos aprobar tu solicitud en este momento. [Reason in plain language.] |
| Disbursement complete | Depositamos $X,XXX en tu cuenta. Puede tardar hasta 60 segundos en aparecer. |
| Payroll deduction ok | Tu cuota de $X fue descontada de esta nómina. |
| Missed deduction | No pudimos descontar tu cuota esta nómina. Contacta a tu empleador. |
| Contract ready | Tu contrato está listo. Fírmalo aquí. |
| Session expired | Tu sesión expiró. Inicia sesión de nuevo. |
| Generic fallback | Algo salió mal. Intenta de nuevo. |

## Microcopy checklist (apply to every user-facing string)

- [ ] Tú, not usted
- [ ] ≤ 16 words
- [ ] Active voice
- [ ] Specific (what happened / what to do)
- [ ] Mexican vocabulary
- [ ] Sentence case
- [ ] No emoji
- [ ] `¿` / `¡` where needed
- [ ] Consistent voice with surrounding copy
- [ ] Peso amounts formatted
- [ ] No "haz clic aquí"
- [ ] No gringo-isms

## When editing existing copy

- Preserve meaning, improve tone. Don't wholesale rewrite working flows without being asked.
- Spanish runs ~20% longer than English — check button widths at 360px with the longer string.
- Regulatory copy → verify with Isaac before shipping changes.
